{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "316",
   "text": "Have Trump's tariffs actually shocked trade flows and the global economy?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "317",
   "text": "A global tariff works like an exchange rate move: import elasticity of about 0.3 to 0.4, not the bilateral elasticity of about 2",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "318",
   "text": "Record tariff revenue means Americans keep importing and paying the tariff",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "319",
   "text": "Tax- and finance-driven flows (pharmaceuticals, gold) are noise; core trade is the real signal",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "320",
   "text": "Annualized trade deficit peaked at $2 trillion in March, fell to $1 trillion, then rebounded to $1.2 trillion in July; imports from Taiwan up over 50 percent year to date; first-term tariffs cut affected trade about 30 percent, and about 50 percent for goods tariffed at 25 percent; high-frequency global trade measures have not slowed",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "321",
   "text": "New York Times reporting; U.S. trade data; federal court ruling on tariff authority",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "322",
   "text": "Pharmaceutical stockpiling (distorted by tax) and gold flows drive the headline swings",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "323",
   "text": "Imports shift from China to Taiwan and Southeast Asia as final assembly relocates",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "324",
   "text": "The data center buildout pushes electronics imports up",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "325",
   "text": "A 15 percent tariff times a 0.3 to 0.4 elasticity cuts imports 5 to 6 percent; non-oil imports fall from about 10 to 9.5 percent of GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#M4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "326",
   "text": "Excluding pharmaceuticals and gold, U.S. imports are roughly on trend; the shock to trade rules far exceeds the shock to trade flows",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "327",
   "text": "The Trump shock to trade flows has not happened yet, though a modest impact should appear",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "328",
   "text": "Reading headline volatility as tariffs crushing trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "329",
   "text": "August deals doubled tariffs on Southeast Asia relative to April; fall data may show more impact; the tariffs' legality is unresolved",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "330",
   "text": "Waiting for tariff relief (autos) replaces front-running; other exporters can take U.S. market share abroad",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2025-09-12_trump-shock-that-wasnt#R1"
  },
